WEBVTT

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:02.336
- Previously on The O.C.:
- What about that date?

00:00:02.545 --> 00:00:04.839
- You're breaking up with me?
- It never could work.

00:00:05.048 --> 00:00:08.052
- Cal, when you wanna date, let me know.
- It was an accident.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.473
You accidentally slept with Marissa's mom
or accidentally told Marissa?

00:00:11.681 --> 00:00:13.141
- I just...
- Get out of here, Luke.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.354
- I don't wanna see him again.
- What about your dad? Kaitlin?

00:00:16.562 --> 00:00:18.273
What am I supposed to do without you?

00:00:18.523 --> 00:00:20.108
You are not leaving this house.

00:00:20.317 --> 00:00:24.113
Or what? You're gonna call the police or
Dr. Milano? You know what? Go ahead.

00:00:24.322 --> 00:00:26.366
In fact, why don't you call up
Dad and Caleb?

00:00:26.575 --> 00:00:28.577
I'd really love to tell them
why I ran away.

00:00:48.686 --> 00:00:50.563
You okay?

00:00:51.398 --> 00:00:54.944
Yeah, it's just really sad.

00:00:56.988 --> 00:01:00.075
It's just the movie, right?
That's the reason for the tears?

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:03.955
Yes. I'm emotionally stable.

00:01:05.207 --> 00:01:07.710
Besides, I'm not the only one crying.

00:01:07.918 --> 00:01:11.005
I'm sorry, what? I'm allergic, okay?

00:01:11.214 --> 00:01:14.051
And there's so much pollen
in here right now. It's ridiculous.

00:01:14.301 --> 00:01:18.515
- Tomorrow we're watching football, okay?
- Football season is five months away.

00:01:18.723 --> 00:01:22.311
ESPN Classics, okay?
We'll watch old games.

00:01:22.854 --> 00:01:24.981
Maybe next time
we should see a comedy.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:28.152
What? No, no. I can see sad movies.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.446
Yeah. No, I know you can.

00:01:30.697 --> 00:01:32.532
I can't, Ryan, I'm sensitive.

00:01:32.741 --> 00:01:35.661
- Okay, so, what now?
- Whatever Coop wants to do.

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:38.999
- Yeah, what do you wanna to do?
- I don't know. It's getting late.

00:01:39.207 --> 00:01:41.961
- So you wanna go back?
- Why don't we have a slumber party.

00:01:42.169 --> 00:01:44.506
- I'll stay over.
- We all will. We'll sleep in shifts.

00:01:44.714 --> 00:01:47.384
- That way, one of us'll be up at all times.
- Doing what?

00:01:47.551 --> 00:01:49.428
Hey, whatever you need us to do.

00:01:49.637 --> 00:01:51.973
- Look, okay? Guys, I'm fine.
- Yeah, yeah. We know.

00:01:52.182 --> 00:01:53.433
Why wouldn't you be?

00:01:53.642 --> 00:01:58.273
I don't know, because the guy I lost
my virginity to had sex with my mom.

00:02:00.401 --> 00:02:04.030
- Oh, yeah, I remember that.
- Look, guys, it's really not that big a deal.

00:02:05.824 --> 00:02:08.911
- Why don't we go to Jamba Juice?
- That's a great idea. I love juice.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:12.290
- Remember that thing with vitamin C?
- The boosts. Free boosts.

00:02:17.046 --> 00:02:18.715
Sit down.

00:02:20.759 --> 00:02:23.596
- Thanks for meeting me.
- Well, it's not like I had any choice.

00:02:23.763 --> 00:02:27.434
All your phone calls and e-mails.
I had to block you from my Buddy List...

00:02:27.643 --> 00:02:30.146
...you were so incessant.
- Blocked me?

00:02:31.147 --> 00:02:34.151
I thought you were off-line.
You want something?

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.404
- The Razzmatazz is...
- Luke...

00:02:36.612 --> 00:02:40.659
...I told you, I'm not staying.
So tell me, what is it that's so important?

00:02:41.118 --> 00:02:43.454
If you drink it too fast,
you can get a brain freeze.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.624
- So sip it slowly.
- That's good advice.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.043
Okay, guys, I can drink a cold beverage.

00:02:48.252 --> 00:02:50.713
I'm telling you, I'm really...

00:02:57.222 --> 00:02:59.766
...so not okay.

00:03:10.905 --> 00:03:13.075
I guess we'll skip the Razzmatazz.

00:03:54.126 --> 00:03:55.962
Hey.

00:03:56.421 --> 00:03:59.299
Sorry. I'm surprised that hasn't
happened before.

00:03:59.508 --> 00:04:02.178
I'm not saying I'm disappointed
it hasn't happened before.

00:04:02.345 --> 00:04:05.640
- I'm saying the mathematical probability...
- Crying during chick flicks.

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:08.310
- Walking in on me getting dressed.
- What's your point?

00:04:08.519 --> 00:04:10.480
I'm not seeing what you're getting at.

00:04:10.814 --> 00:04:13.108
- Do you work out?
- Not really.

00:04:13.317 --> 00:04:15.236
Me neither.
I'm gonna go watch some hockey.

00:04:15.444 --> 00:04:17.697
- Hockey season's over.
- Damn it.

00:04:17.906 --> 00:04:21.285
- Where you going?
- To find Luke. Beat the crap out of him.

00:04:21.619 --> 00:04:25.582
- Where'll the can of whup-ass be opened?
- I'll go to his house, check the pier.

00:04:25.791 --> 00:04:28.169
Have you considered our back yard?

00:04:28.377 --> 00:04:30.254
- What's up, guys?
- Why don't you tell me?

00:04:30.463 --> 00:04:33.342
- Calm down. I didn't come to fight.
- You told me it was over.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:37.388
It is. Believe me.
I just... I had to talk to her.

00:04:37.597 --> 00:04:40.935
Next time you wanna talk to somebody,
talk to Seth, me. Anyone but her.

00:04:41.143 --> 00:04:42.687
No one will talk to me.

00:04:42.854 --> 00:04:46.024
Sleeping with your ex-girlfriend's mom
kind of yields that result.

00:04:46.233 --> 00:04:48.694
- I thought you were my friends.
- You got no friends.

00:04:49.195 --> 00:04:50.947
I know.

00:04:52.157 --> 00:04:54.827
- But I need your help.
- I'm not gonna help you.

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:56.871
- I'm leaving.
- Thanks for stopping by.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.665
No, I mean, I'm leaving town.

00:05:00.125 --> 00:05:03.463
Now that the divorce is final,
my dad just wants to get out, so...

00:05:04.881 --> 00:05:07.593
- We got family in Portland.
- You're going with him?

00:05:10.138 --> 00:05:13.100
Don't tell anybody.
But that's what I was trying to tell Julie.

00:05:13.308 --> 00:05:17.063
And that's what I wanna tell Marissa.
But I wanna tell her myself.

00:05:17.272 --> 00:05:20.442
- Look, I don't know, Luke.
- Come on. Please, please. Five minutes.

00:05:20.651 --> 00:05:23.321
It's not that much to ask,
to say goodbye.

00:05:23.488 --> 00:05:25.115
Then I'm gone.

00:05:26.033 --> 00:05:27.409
Please.

00:05:28.953 --> 00:05:30.914
- You okay?
- Yeah, just checking the paper...

00:05:31.122 --> 00:05:35.586
...for any impending natural disasters
before tomorrow's grand opening.

00:05:35.795 --> 00:05:38.173
- You're not nervous, are you?
- No, why be nervous?

00:05:38.381 --> 00:05:40.759
If our pre-celebration tonight
goes badly...

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:43.763
...there'll be no time
to fix it before tomorrow night.

00:05:43.972 --> 00:05:46.475
I like to anticipate the worst at all times.

00:05:46.683 --> 00:05:49.020
It's a Cohen family trait.

00:05:49.228 --> 00:05:51.982
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

00:05:56.946 --> 00:05:59.366
- Yes!
- What is that?

00:05:59.574 --> 00:06:02.411
- We're business partners.
- We needed our own secret handshake.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:05.540
- Secret handshake?
- It's a guy thing.

00:06:05.749 --> 00:06:08.711
- You couldn't possibly understand.
- Is this okay?

00:06:09.045 --> 00:06:11.506
Or is it putting the "ho" in hostess?

00:06:11.715 --> 00:06:14.844
Hailey, it looks great.
But it's not my restaurant.

00:06:15.219 --> 00:06:16.846
Jimmy?

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:21.060
Yeah. Yeah. No, I mean...

00:06:21.268 --> 00:06:24.022
...we should ask Sandy because...
- I don't have shoes.

00:06:24.397 --> 00:06:28.527
It'll serve to distract the customers, which
is good, since they won't be drinking.

00:06:28.736 --> 00:06:31.406
The Liquor Board is reneging
on our liquor license.

00:06:31.615 --> 00:06:35.953
- They can't. They gave us a permit.
- Must be a mix-up. I'll call the inspector.

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:39.625
See, that's why we Cohens
are always right.

00:06:39.791 --> 00:06:42.169
Because the worst always happens.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:45.090
Come on, Hail. I'll go get your shoes.

00:06:47.426 --> 00:06:49.387
So you like the dress?

00:06:49.595 --> 00:06:51.890
It's definitely a keeper.

00:06:52.098 --> 00:06:54.518
So you'd sit in my section?

00:06:55.811 --> 00:06:58.899
How do you even make waitress-speak
sound so...?

00:06:59.107 --> 00:07:00.693
Dirty?

00:07:01.318 --> 00:07:04.447
I was gonna say "untoward," but, yeah.

00:07:05.073 --> 00:07:09.287
Hail, it's your feet, not mine.

00:07:11.539 --> 00:07:13.208
Can you believe this?

00:07:17.088 --> 00:07:19.549
Okay, Coop. So...

00:07:19.758 --> 00:07:21.677
...what's it gonna be, a little salt glow?

00:07:21.927 --> 00:07:25.265
Little Tahitian body wrap?
Or maybe a lotion boot?

00:07:25.474 --> 00:07:27.685
Okay, not really into exfoliating
right now.

00:07:27.893 --> 00:07:31.106
Besides, I promised Ryan
I'd meet him for lunch at the pier.

00:07:31.314 --> 00:07:35.236
Lunch at the pier. Corn dogs and pizza.
You know, I read an article in Stuff.

00:07:35.444 --> 00:07:38.615
It says carbs send endorphins
to your brain and that makes you happy.

00:07:38.824 --> 00:07:42.370
Oh, that's probably Ryan.
I gotta go grab it.

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:45.207
Where'd you leave your phone?
Your dad's room?

00:07:45.499 --> 00:07:46.708
No, my room.

00:07:46.917 --> 00:07:48.836
You have a room?

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:51.047
Wait.

00:07:52.215 --> 00:07:53.759
Hello?

00:07:53.967 --> 00:07:56.262
Yeah, Coop.
Like what you've done with the place.

00:07:57.305 --> 00:08:00.768
Yeah, I guess I didn't really get around
to unpacking.

00:08:01.185 --> 00:08:03.980
How can you live like this?
Your T-shirts touch your sweaters.

00:08:04.189 --> 00:08:08.569
I figured that if I didn't hang anything up
then it wouldn't be so permanent.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.032
Anyway, I gotta go meet Ryan.
So do you wanna come or...?

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.578
You know what? Do you mind
if I hang out here and watch TV?

00:08:15.786 --> 00:08:19.374
The step-monster got her wisdom teeth
pulled. She's whacked out on Percocet...

00:08:19.583 --> 00:08:24.923
...leaving drool all over the house.
- Okay, sure. Go ahead. I'll see you later.

00:08:33.308 --> 00:08:36.604
- I can't believe they're seeing each other.
- They're not.

00:08:36.813 --> 00:08:41.068
- That's not what it looked like last night.
- Last night wasn't what it looked like.

00:08:41.944 --> 00:08:44.155
I talked to Luke.

00:08:44.447 --> 00:08:47.201
What? You guys are still hanging out?

00:08:47.409 --> 00:08:50.997
No, he showed up.
He wants to talk to you. Apologize.

00:08:51.206 --> 00:08:52.749
No.

00:08:52.958 --> 00:08:56.128
There's no way I could forgive him.

00:08:56.337 --> 00:09:00.092
- Maybe for Holly. But not for this.
- I know...

00:09:00.384 --> 00:09:02.386
...but it would mean a lot to him.

00:09:03.763 --> 00:09:08.185
What's important to him
is really not so important to me.

00:09:10.438 --> 00:09:13.358
That's a whole part of my life
I'd just rather keep separate...

00:09:13.567 --> 00:09:16.237
...from this part of my life.

00:09:29.754 --> 00:09:31.715
You know what we haven't done
in a while?

00:09:55.745 --> 00:09:58.540
Listen, I'm all for getting it on
in exotic locales.

00:09:58.748 --> 00:10:02.587
But I think your best friend's
bedroom's just really disheveled.

00:10:02.795 --> 00:10:05.799
Wow. I like what she's done
with the place.

00:10:06.008 --> 00:10:08.594
The cardboard boxes, it feels very...

00:10:08.761 --> 00:10:10.680
I'm getting like a garage-sale vibe.

00:10:10.889 --> 00:10:15.311
Yes, I know. See, they say your
external life influences your internal life.

00:10:15.519 --> 00:10:17.647
- Who says that?
- I read it in ELLE Decor.

00:10:17.856 --> 00:10:20.067
- Your favorite magazine.
- You read?

00:10:20.275 --> 00:10:23.571
No wonder she's so depressed.
We need to surprise her and fix it up.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:26.867
Do you think giving her a little
feng shui will help her forget...

00:10:27.076 --> 00:10:29.746
...her mom slept with her ex-boyfriend?
- It can't hurt.

00:10:29.912 --> 00:10:32.666
Right. Well, that's very sweet.

00:10:33.292 --> 00:10:38.465
But if you put a mirror on that wall,
it'd open up the energy flow in this room.

00:10:38.673 --> 00:10:41.343
- I know where you're going with this.
- The hardware store.

00:10:42.136 --> 00:10:45.724
The hardware store? With, like, the bolts
and the grouting and the Skil saws?

00:10:45.932 --> 00:10:49.061
You don't like hardware stores
and you cry during chick flicks.

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:53.108
Next thing you're gonna tell me,
you walk in on Ryan changing.

00:10:53.525 --> 00:10:57.280
Come on. That's crazy.
Hey, let's go to the hardware store.

00:10:59.074 --> 00:11:02.078
Peter Johnson, from the Liquor Board.
Am I right?

00:11:02.286 --> 00:11:05.457
You came here about a month ago
and granted us a liquor license.

00:11:05.665 --> 00:11:10.588
Craziest thing. I open my mail, and I read
that our liquor license had been reneged.

00:11:10.797 --> 00:11:12.007
Yes.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:16.387
- Yeah, crazy?
- Yes, your license has been reneged.

00:11:18.807 --> 00:11:21.727
Without a liquor license,
this place can't turn a profit.

00:11:21.936 --> 00:11:24.606
This is Newport Beach.
Everyone's a borderline alcoholic.

00:11:24.814 --> 00:11:27.151
I'm sorry, but your temporary license
was issued...

00:11:27.359 --> 00:11:30.655
...before your file landed in front of
the newly appointed commissioner.

00:11:30.864 --> 00:11:34.785
- So?
- The name Steve Peiser mean anything?

00:11:34.994 --> 00:11:36.537
No.

00:11:36.746 --> 00:11:39.332
Well, it might to Jimmy Cooper.

00:11:39.541 --> 00:11:42.920
Turns out Mr. Cooper was
Commissioner Peiser's financial advisor...

00:11:43.129 --> 00:11:45.799
...before he stole a quarter
of a million dollars from him.

00:11:45.966 --> 00:11:46.967
You're kidding me.

00:11:47.301 --> 00:11:51.640
It was that financial loss that forced my
boss out of retirement and back to work.

00:11:51.848 --> 00:11:54.685
He saw Cooper's name on the file
and said "no way."

00:11:54.977 --> 00:11:57.897
Want my advice?
Have Mr. Cooper step down.

00:12:04.614 --> 00:12:06.617
So, what do you wanna do for lunch?

00:12:06.825 --> 00:12:09.996
I can do mac and cheese
or mac and cheese.

00:12:10.204 --> 00:12:11.998
Tough choice.

00:12:20.134 --> 00:12:23.888
- I forgot how fun this was.
- Pretty fun.

00:12:24.806 --> 00:12:26.975
You know, lunch could wait.

00:12:27.184 --> 00:12:29.729
We are having a pretty big dinner.

00:12:32.149 --> 00:12:36.154
- Not your dad, is it?
- No, he has a key.

00:12:44.914 --> 00:12:47.459
- Mr. Nichol.
- Call me Caleb.

00:12:47.668 --> 00:12:49.879
I'm not disturbing you, am I?

00:12:50.338 --> 00:12:52.215
No. Yeah, come in.

00:12:53.342 --> 00:12:55.553
- Ryan.
- Mr. Nichol.

00:12:55.761 --> 00:12:58.181
Would you mind if Marissa
and I had a word, privately?

00:12:59.141 --> 00:13:02.478
- Sure.
- Actually, Ryan and I don't have secrets.

00:13:03.813 --> 00:13:05.607
It's important.

00:13:05.816 --> 00:13:07.526
Well, then I definitely want him here.

00:13:11.156 --> 00:13:14.493
What follows doesn't leave
this room then, okay?

00:13:14.702 --> 00:13:16.329
Sit down.

00:13:19.875 --> 00:13:22.420
Marissa, your mother's
a wonderful woman.

00:13:22.628 --> 00:13:23.880
She is?

00:13:24.547 --> 00:13:27.885
You're important to her. You and I
haven't spent a lot of time together...

00:13:28.093 --> 00:13:31.389
...but it was important to me
to come and get your blessing.

00:13:32.683 --> 00:13:35.019
I'm gonna ask her to marry me.

00:13:38.857 --> 00:13:41.694
- You wanna marry my mom?
- I love her very much.

00:13:41.902 --> 00:13:44.614
- You don't know her.
- You should give Marissa some time.

00:13:44.823 --> 00:13:47.409
- This is kind of a big deal.
- Impossible.

00:13:50.413 --> 00:13:52.958
I intend to propose to her
tonight at the restaurant...

00:13:53.166 --> 00:13:56.003
...with our friends and family
in attendance.

00:13:59.341 --> 00:14:01.385
Well, then I guess I can't stop you.

00:14:01.594 --> 00:14:03.429
I'll see you both tonight.

00:14:03.638 --> 00:14:05.974
Thanks for your time, dear.

00:14:06.183 --> 00:14:08.936
And again, this is just between us.

00:14:09.103 --> 00:14:11.314
I want it to be a surprise.

00:14:19.282 --> 00:14:23.037
If my mom marries him, she's gonna be
the most powerful woman in Newport.

00:14:25.373 --> 00:14:27.918
Not if you tell Caleb the truth.

00:14:39.099 --> 00:14:41.769
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:14:41.977 --> 00:14:44.230
- Did you talk to her?
- I tried.

00:14:44.439 --> 00:14:46.900
- And?
- I don't think it's gonna happen, man.

00:14:47.109 --> 00:14:51.072
- What do you mean?
- She's dealing with a lot of stuff now.

00:14:51.281 --> 00:14:53.951
- Family stuff.
- She won't even see me for 30 seconds?

00:14:54.118 --> 00:14:57.580
Her dad's restaurant's having its
private opening tonight. She's busy.

00:14:57.789 --> 00:14:59.583
- I'm leaving town.
- She doesn't know.

00:14:59.791 --> 00:15:03.713
- That's because she won't talk to me.
- Why don't you just write her a letter?

00:15:04.088 --> 00:15:06.049
Write her a letter?

00:15:09.053 --> 00:15:11.765
- I had your back with Oliver.
- You had sex with her mom.

00:15:11.973 --> 00:15:14.852
I didn't just have sex with her, okay?!
I'm in love with her!

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.105
- I was... I am in love!
- Don't need to hear it.

00:15:17.313 --> 00:15:20.067
But Marissa does. I have to talk to her.
I have to explain.

00:15:20.275 --> 00:15:23.363
- Luke, I wouldn't.
- I can't go without making it right.

00:15:23.988 --> 00:15:25.657
I won't.

00:15:32.916 --> 00:15:36.504
Okay, the plan is, we go to dinner
for, like, 10 minutes, right?

00:15:36.713 --> 00:15:40.134
Then we sneak out, come back here
and make magic happen.

00:15:40.342 --> 00:15:45.098
Excellent. I'm extremely stealth.
1996, All-School Hide-and-Seek champion.

00:15:45.307 --> 00:15:49.520
I do believe Joel Gordon
is still looking for me. The fool.

00:15:49.812 --> 00:15:52.941
Hey! Last year's yearbook.

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:55.528
- God, I love yearbooks.
- Listen, let's put it away...

00:15:55.736 --> 00:15:57.822
...because we've got
a lot of work to do.

00:15:58.031 --> 00:16:00.534
- Stop it!
- Let's just put it back.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:07.209
Hey, it's you.

00:16:08.919 --> 00:16:13.342
- We had a sailing team?
- Yeah. It never got off the ground, but...

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:19.015
- You were in the Comic Book Club?
- I was the president and only member.

00:16:19.516 --> 00:16:20.768
Let's see.

00:16:22.687 --> 00:16:25.941
- We had a Film Preservation Society?
- Yeah, but it was a long time ago.

00:16:26.149 --> 00:16:28.819
So you know, we don't have to...

00:16:29.028 --> 00:16:30.655
It's not fun.

00:16:32.866 --> 00:16:34.159
Was I really mean to you?

00:16:38.039 --> 00:16:39.666
No.

00:16:39.875 --> 00:16:42.712
That would have required you
to speak to me.

00:16:45.715 --> 00:16:47.968
Or anyone to speak to me.

00:16:51.681 --> 00:16:54.518
A lot's changed in a year, huh?

00:17:04.781 --> 00:17:06.325
Hey.

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:11.081
"Marissa, you're the greatest.
This summer will rock.

00:17:11.289 --> 00:17:14.835
- Love you forever, Luke."
- Yeah.

00:17:15.044 --> 00:17:17.797
A lot's definitely changed.

00:17:18.506 --> 00:17:21.302
Marissa's gonna need
a whole lot of feng shui.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.124
Hey. You look beautiful.

00:17:46.333 --> 00:17:47.960
Thank you.

00:17:48.294 --> 00:17:50.380
You look sad.

00:17:51.005 --> 00:17:53.217
I thought this would be
a moment to celebrate.

00:17:53.425 --> 00:17:54.802
So did I.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:57.222
You know that mix-up
with the liquor license?

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.641
- It's not such a mix-up.
- You're kidding.

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:03.146
It turns out the new commissioner
is a former client of Jimmy's...

00:18:03.354 --> 00:18:05.565
...with a quarter-million dollar
score to settle.

00:18:05.774 --> 00:18:07.985
Without that license,
there's no point opening.

00:18:08.194 --> 00:18:11.990
I've been on the phone trying to call in
favors. I got nothing. The guy is serious.

00:18:12.199 --> 00:18:16.162
The only way he'll reconsider is if
Jimmy steps down. Leaves the business.

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:19.583
- You're not considering...
- No, of course not.

00:18:20.876 --> 00:18:24.422
Well, there is one last option.
You're not gonna like it.

00:18:24.631 --> 00:18:26.466
My dad can be very...

00:18:26.675 --> 00:18:28.469
He can be very persuasive.

00:18:28.719 --> 00:18:32.432
I may have to throw a few more of these
back before you start bringing up Caleb.

00:18:32.891 --> 00:18:34.810
Desperate times.

00:18:35.019 --> 00:18:37.021
This is that.

00:19:05.056 --> 00:19:07.434
Hey, man. What's going on?

00:19:07.643 --> 00:19:09.520
- Where you been?
- What?

00:19:09.729 --> 00:19:11.648
- What?
- What's going on?

00:19:11.856 --> 00:19:14.401
- Nothing. Not one thing, okay?
- All right.

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:27.835
I'm gonna go pee, okay? So if anyone
asks, that's where I am. For a while.

00:19:28.043 --> 00:19:29.504
Right.

00:19:30.213 --> 00:19:33.467
- He's getting weirder.
- Didn't think that was possible.

00:19:33.675 --> 00:19:35.344
Marissa.

00:19:35.553 --> 00:19:37.138
Mom.

00:19:42.061 --> 00:19:44.731
That's the warmest conversation
I've had with her in weeks.

00:19:44.898 --> 00:19:47.192
I'll have a word, see if I can't help.

00:19:47.401 --> 00:19:49.445
I have been known
to be quite persuasive.

00:19:49.654 --> 00:19:51.698
So I've heard.

00:19:55.202 --> 00:19:58.540
What's with Dad these days?
He's all warm and mushy.

00:19:58.748 --> 00:20:00.167
Don't know.

00:20:00.375 --> 00:20:03.671
Maybe it's the new
blood-thinning medication he's on.

00:20:04.506 --> 00:20:06.967
What about you?
How's your romantic life?

00:20:08.093 --> 00:20:10.805
Oh, you know me. Not much.

00:20:11.514 --> 00:20:12.724
Vince, thank you so much.

00:20:13.517 --> 00:20:15.311
How excited is Jimmy?

00:20:15.686 --> 00:20:18.440
He's like a totally different person.

00:20:18.732 --> 00:20:20.734
It's so great.

00:20:21.777 --> 00:20:24.531
Let's hope tomorrow night
goes as well as tonight.

00:20:24.739 --> 00:20:28.160
- Pat. Thanks for coming by.
- My pleasure.

00:20:28.369 --> 00:20:32.833
Though I gotta say, Nana Cohen's
meat loaf, trouncing Grandma Cooper's.

00:20:33.041 --> 00:20:36.462
- She would expect no less.
- How'd it go today with the Liquor Board?

00:20:36.671 --> 00:20:39.883
- All sorted out?
- Working on it. Working on it.

00:20:40.092 --> 00:20:43.137
Enjoy it, Jimmy. Moments like this
don't happen every day.

00:20:43.346 --> 00:20:44.723
I know.

00:20:45.348 --> 00:20:47.309
It's fantastic.

00:21:14.051 --> 00:21:16.471
- Hey.
- How you doing?

00:21:17.055 --> 00:21:20.225
I'm just happy you're here,
so I don't have to do this alone.

00:21:20.434 --> 00:21:22.937
You know me.
Can't get enough of this stuff.

00:21:27.359 --> 00:21:30.029
Excuse me, everyone.
I have something I'd like to say.

00:21:31.072 --> 00:21:34.034
I hope you're all enjoying yourselves
tonight as much as I am.

00:21:34.243 --> 00:21:38.164
Though my enjoyment of life over the last
few months goes beyond this restaurant...

00:21:38.373 --> 00:21:40.751
...to a very special lady, Julie Cooper.

00:21:46.383 --> 00:21:48.093
What's he doing here?

00:21:48.385 --> 00:21:51.848
Julie did a fantastic job
on the d Ácor, didn't she?

00:21:54.059 --> 00:21:55.603
Hey, come on, let's go.

00:21:55.811 --> 00:21:57.021
And...

00:21:57.272 --> 00:22:00.818
- It's here on this opening night...
- Nobody'll talk to me or even look at me.

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:04.864
- Had a little bit to drink?
- I'd like to show her how special she is.

00:22:05.073 --> 00:22:08.369
I gotta tell Marissa it wasn't just sex.
I love her mom.

00:22:08.577 --> 00:22:10.997
Okay, I don't think that's a good idea.

00:22:17.547 --> 00:22:19.091
Julie Cooper...

00:22:20.551 --> 00:22:22.094
...will you marry me?

00:22:24.389 --> 00:22:26.350
Oh, my God!

00:22:28.894 --> 00:22:31.648
Yes, of course I will, Cal.

00:22:39.866 --> 00:22:42.244
Kiki!

00:22:48.043 --> 00:22:51.172
Luke. Hey. Luke. Hey!

00:22:51.548 --> 00:22:53.217
- Look, Luke...
- Don't make me!

00:22:53.425 --> 00:22:55.720
Just give me your keys.
Let me drive you home.

00:22:56.053 --> 00:22:57.555
What home?

00:23:19.917 --> 00:23:21.794
I can't believe he just showed up here.

00:23:22.003 --> 00:23:24.673
- I need your car. I need to go after him.
- No.

00:23:25.215 --> 00:23:27.217
It's like you're saying
he did nothing wrong.

00:23:27.426 --> 00:23:29.637
I'm not taking his side.
I'm not taking any side.

00:23:29.846 --> 00:23:31.389
You know what? Maybe you should.

00:23:31.598 --> 00:23:34.059
He should have time alone
to think about what he did.

00:23:34.268 --> 00:23:37.355
- Feel bad about it.
- He does feel bad...

00:23:37.564 --> 00:23:40.234
- That's why he's leaving.
- What are you talking about?

00:23:40.776 --> 00:23:45.073
His dad's moving to Portland. He's moving
with him. Because of what happened.

00:23:46.867 --> 00:23:50.288
Can I have your keys?
He's had a lot to drink.

00:23:58.673 --> 00:24:02.678
- That's cool. I didn't want any, anyway.
- My dad is marrying Julie Cooper.

00:24:02.845 --> 00:24:05.557
Julie Cooper is my stepmom.

00:24:05.766 --> 00:24:07.851
- Maybe we'll get you another bottle.
- Drink up.

00:24:08.060 --> 00:24:12.649
This is an unholy alliance, two storm
fronts colliding. It's the apocalypse for us.

00:24:13.233 --> 00:24:15.486
- Maybe you wanna lay off the sauce.
- Think of it.

00:24:15.695 --> 00:24:18.573
All the time we were growing up
and you'd come over for dinner...

00:24:18.782 --> 00:24:23.329
...you'd go sailing with my dad, did you
ever think he would marry your ex-wife?

00:24:23.538 --> 00:24:25.123
- Yeah, give me a glass.
- Never.

00:24:25.332 --> 00:24:29.337
Jimbo, the way I see it, this might be
the best thing that could happen to you.

00:24:29.545 --> 00:24:32.549
There is nothing good about it.
This marriage is an asteroid...

00:24:32.758 --> 00:24:35.720
...that hit the Earth. Now we
have to see what species survives.

00:24:40.517 --> 00:24:42.812
I did it. Look.

00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:46.692
Wow, you hit a nail!
Bob Vila's your bitch, Cohen.

00:24:49.195 --> 00:24:51.281
What?! Why?!

00:24:51.489 --> 00:24:54.410
- This is not supposed to happen.
- You have to find the stud.

00:24:56.955 --> 00:25:00.083
- You mean like you did, Summer?
- Just get me the stud finder.

00:25:00.292 --> 00:25:03.546
Oh, Summer,
I think you are the stud finder.

00:25:03.755 --> 00:25:06.884
- See this hammer in my hand?
- What does the stud finder look like?

00:25:07.092 --> 00:25:08.552
- And the level.
- What is a level?

00:25:08.761 --> 00:25:11.598
- Don't you know what a level is?
- What you advance to in a video game.

00:25:11.806 --> 00:25:15.895
That's funny. Yeah.
The tool doesn't know about tools.

00:25:16.103 --> 00:25:20.150
My people, we don't really build.
We're not what you would call "handy."

00:25:20.359 --> 00:25:23.655
We hire people to do it.
Why don't we just get a contractor?

00:25:24.656 --> 00:25:27.159
Or I can paint.

00:25:28.369 --> 00:25:30.663
And here I thought
you could only paint the ceiling.

00:26:09.253 --> 00:26:11.131
Marissa, hey, listen, l...

00:26:11.339 --> 00:26:12.549
No, no. It's me, man.

00:26:14.552 --> 00:26:17.096
- I'm fine, man.
- You don't sound fine.

00:26:17.597 --> 00:26:22.270
Well, you know, I'm just having
a few beers up at the park...

00:26:22.478 --> 00:26:24.439
...rocking out to Seger.
You know the drill.

00:26:24.647 --> 00:26:25.899
Not really.

00:26:26.149 --> 00:26:28.527
Hey, do me a favor, Ryan.

00:26:28.903 --> 00:26:30.363
Tell Marissa I get it.

00:26:31.531 --> 00:26:35.077
Okay? I don 't deserve her forgiveness.

00:26:35.286 --> 00:26:36.746
I'm...

00:26:36.913 --> 00:26:39.207
I'm scum. I'm...

00:26:39.416 --> 00:26:42.503
All I ever did was let her down.
Tell her that.

00:26:42.712 --> 00:26:45.382
No, just tell me where you are, all right?

00:26:45.590 --> 00:26:47.801
You can't leave
without saying goodbye, right?

00:26:48.010 --> 00:26:49.512
Right.

00:26:50.179 --> 00:26:51.765
Goodbye.

00:27:06.783 --> 00:27:08.869
Damn it!

00:27:26.558 --> 00:27:28.894
I'm not here. Leave a message.

00:27:29.103 --> 00:27:30.730
Julie.

00:27:30.897 --> 00:27:32.482
I'm...

00:27:32.691 --> 00:27:34.360
I'm leaving tomorrow.

00:27:35.194 --> 00:27:37.864
I need to see you.

00:27:40.284 --> 00:27:43.705
I'm coming... I'm coming to see you.

00:27:45.123 --> 00:27:47.710
You owe me a goodbye!

00:27:54.426 --> 00:27:57.138
Without a liquor license,
we'll be belly-up in no time.

00:27:57.347 --> 00:28:00.476
- Really? Cal, I had no idea.
- There's no point in opening the place.

00:28:00.684 --> 00:28:03.229
That's why I was hoping
I could ask you to do me a favor.

00:28:03.438 --> 00:28:05.607
- What?
- Wait, did you not hear me?

00:28:05.816 --> 00:28:07.693
I just wanted to hear you say it again.

00:28:08.110 --> 00:28:11.865
If it was up to me, I'd rather take the hit
than talk with you. But it's Jimmy.

00:28:12.073 --> 00:28:15.995
- The Lighthouse is all he's got.
- Lf you drop him, they'd issue the license.

00:28:16.579 --> 00:28:19.791
But you're too much of a martyr.
Listen, Sanford...

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:22.420
...never mix business with friendship.
- You're right.

00:28:22.628 --> 00:28:24.881
From now on,
I'm doing all my deals with you.

00:28:25.215 --> 00:28:28.511
When you came to me about Uncle Shaun,
I said yes. You owe me.

00:28:28.719 --> 00:28:31.264
I don't wanna owe you.
I wanna hold it over your head.

00:28:32.849 --> 00:28:36.521
Need water. Tried to lie down,
got the spins.

00:28:36.729 --> 00:28:39.065
Well, I better get back to my bride-to-be.

00:28:39.274 --> 00:28:42.153
Oh, yeah. Definitely might vomit.

00:28:44.280 --> 00:28:46.491
Luke, call us when you get this.

00:30:02.461 --> 00:30:04.214
Ryan.

00:30:09.887 --> 00:30:13.058
When I saw him at the party last night...

00:30:13.517 --> 00:30:15.603
...I wished for something like this
to happen.

00:30:15.811 --> 00:30:17.522
It's not your fault.

00:30:21.736 --> 00:30:24.280
- How is he?
- Well, he's out of surgery.

00:30:24.531 --> 00:30:28.285
He's pretty much out of commission
right now, but the worst is behind him.

00:30:28.494 --> 00:30:30.580
I should call my parents.

00:30:31.247 --> 00:30:32.749
You guys...

00:30:32.958 --> 00:30:36.504
...he's gonna be asleep for a while.
You should go home.

00:30:38.173 --> 00:30:41.677
- Maybe we should, so we could finish.
- Or we could sleep.

00:30:42.053 --> 00:30:45.432
You know, I'm really glad
that Luke's gonna be okay.

00:30:45.640 --> 00:30:47.434
We'll come back.

00:30:51.481 --> 00:30:55.111
Actually, I'm gonna stay.
You know, just in case.

00:30:58.949 --> 00:31:00.659
Okay.

00:31:02.286 --> 00:31:04.289
Then I'll stay too.

00:31:05.832 --> 00:31:07.209
I heard he'd been drinking...

00:31:07.918 --> 00:31:11.089
...which makes one less inspired
to go after our liquor license.

00:31:11.297 --> 00:31:13.592
- Can I get you something to eat?
- No, no, I'm good.

00:31:13.801 --> 00:31:17.764
Don't worry about going to city hall. I'll
deal with them. You hold down the fort.

00:31:17.972 --> 00:31:21.060
That's not necessary.
You hang at the Lighthouse. Man the ship.

00:31:21.268 --> 00:31:24.814
Are we gonna refer to the restaurant
as a ship or a fort?

00:31:25.023 --> 00:31:26.859
Well, right now it's a sinking ship.

00:31:27.067 --> 00:31:31.281
Okay, not the most inspiring metaphor
on our opening night.

00:31:32.115 --> 00:31:33.325
Why don't you sit down?

00:31:33.534 --> 00:31:37.163
I can't. I gotta go see what the holdup is
with the liquor license.

00:31:38.999 --> 00:31:40.167
You're the holdup, Jimmy.

00:31:40.960 --> 00:31:43.838
Does the name Steve Peiser
mean anything to you?

00:31:44.172 --> 00:31:48.970
When he went back to work, after his
financial advisor lost his life savings...

00:31:49.846 --> 00:31:53.225
...he got a job
as commissioner of the Liquor Board.

00:31:56.980 --> 00:31:59.483
This restaurant was supposed to be...

00:31:59.691 --> 00:32:01.652
...a chance for me...

00:32:03.529 --> 00:32:05.949
...to escape from my past.

00:32:06.158 --> 00:32:08.202
I guess there is no escaping, huh?

00:32:08.411 --> 00:32:12.958
Well, we do have one possible
Houdini-esque escape left.

00:32:14.710 --> 00:32:16.295
Caleb.

00:32:16.504 --> 00:32:17.922
I asked him for help.

00:32:18.798 --> 00:32:22.178
- You hate asking him for help.
- This was no exception. I had no choice.

00:32:22.428 --> 00:32:25.390
You did. You could've told me
the truth and asked me to bow out.

00:32:25.849 --> 00:32:28.436
Like I said, I had no choice.

00:32:30.814 --> 00:32:33.317
Satellite Pharmacy to room 607.

00:32:33.525 --> 00:32:36.821
Satellite Pharmacy, room 607.

00:32:47.918 --> 00:32:51.339
Hey, guys. He's up.

00:32:51.882 --> 00:32:56.512
You should go home.
And thanks for waiting, all right?

00:32:58.723 --> 00:33:00.517
Wait.

00:33:03.020 --> 00:33:05.982
Will you tell him that I'm here...

00:33:06.567 --> 00:33:08.110
...and I'd like to see him?

00:33:12.950 --> 00:33:15.035
I'll start auditioning bands right away.

00:33:15.244 --> 00:33:18.248
I need to start soliciting
recommendations for the videographer...

00:33:18.456 --> 00:33:21.961
...and the photographer, the engravers.
You know, I should ask Diane Kahn.

00:33:22.169 --> 00:33:24.965
She's been married, like,
at least a half a dozen times.

00:33:25.173 --> 00:33:27.092
Why aren't you more excited?

00:33:27.885 --> 00:33:30.138
Oh, Julie, it was a rough night.

00:33:33.392 --> 00:33:35.645
Hey, where are you going?
Why aren't you asleep?

00:33:35.853 --> 00:33:37.605
Because Summer's a slave driver.

00:33:38.857 --> 00:33:40.859
Is Ryan back from the hospital yet?

00:33:41.068 --> 00:33:43.738
- Hospital?
- Oh, didn't you hear?

00:33:43.905 --> 00:33:47.242
Luke wrapped his truck
around a telephone pole last night.

00:33:47.868 --> 00:33:50.455
- He did?
- Just a few blocks from here.

00:33:50.663 --> 00:33:54.209
He was drinking. So unlike him.

00:33:58.214 --> 00:34:00.342
Well, I guess he just...

00:34:00.551 --> 00:34:03.554
...never really recovered
from everything with his father.

00:34:05.432 --> 00:34:08.561
You know, the humiliation,
his family being torn apart.

00:34:09.979 --> 00:34:12.023
Yeah, that must be it.

00:34:14.652 --> 00:34:18.824
Pour me a bloody mary, will you, James?
Since it'll be the last drink we serve.

00:34:19.032 --> 00:34:22.537
- What? That's it?
- Hook, line and sinker.

00:34:22.745 --> 00:34:24.956
No license. No opening. No restaurant.

00:34:25.248 --> 00:34:27.334
- No comeback.
- That's the best you could do?

00:34:27.543 --> 00:34:32.758
- As big a badass as you are?
- Didn't have an effect on this Peiser fella.

00:34:33.217 --> 00:34:36.345
You know how to piss people off.
You could teach me a thing or two.

00:34:36.554 --> 00:34:39.516
- You seem awfully glib.
- Everything happens for a reason.

00:34:39.933 --> 00:34:42.854
Could you at least feign
a little sensitivity at our misfortune?

00:34:43.062 --> 00:34:46.942
You know what they say: One man's
misfortune is another man's fortune.

00:34:47.693 --> 00:34:50.113
- Who says that?
- I do.

00:34:50.822 --> 00:34:53.367
- I've never seen him smile.
- I didn't know he had teeth.

00:34:53.575 --> 00:34:56.788
Make yourselves a couple of drinks,
fellas. We should talk.

00:34:56.996 --> 00:34:58.248
Cheers.

00:35:17.605 --> 00:35:19.608
Are you okay?

00:35:21.402 --> 00:35:23.321
I'm so sorry.

00:35:23.529 --> 00:35:25.991
I didn't mean for this to happen.

00:35:27.493 --> 00:35:29.370
Any of it.

00:35:30.747 --> 00:35:32.374
I just...

00:35:33.125 --> 00:35:36.921
I didn't have anyone.
I had no one. Not my family.

00:35:38.256 --> 00:35:40.718
I don't know, you know?

00:35:46.266 --> 00:35:47.810
But...

00:35:49.937 --> 00:35:51.272
...I'm gonna go away.

00:35:54.318 --> 00:35:57.864
Give things a chance
to go back to normal for you.

00:35:58.490 --> 00:36:02.411
Because I know
as long as I'm here, they won't.

00:36:10.213 --> 00:36:12.257
But I need to know one thing
before I go.

00:36:18.765 --> 00:36:20.893
Can you forgive me?

00:36:24.439 --> 00:36:26.024
Yeah.

00:36:26.733 --> 00:36:27.943
Yes.

00:36:35.411 --> 00:36:37.205
Luke...

00:36:40.960 --> 00:36:42.169
...I'll miss you.

00:37:11.122 --> 00:37:14.293
Who would've thought
when you moved to town...

00:37:14.501 --> 00:37:16.838
...that I'd be the one who had to leave?

00:37:17.046 --> 00:37:20.175
I thought I was gonna live in Newport
my whole life.

00:37:20.384 --> 00:37:22.553
So you'll start a new life.

00:37:23.262 --> 00:37:26.058
Yeah, maybe I'll show up in Portland...

00:37:26.809 --> 00:37:30.271
...and fall for the chick dating
the captain of the football team.

00:37:30.480 --> 00:37:32.357
And he can kick your ass.

00:37:34.735 --> 00:37:36.696
Yeah.

00:37:36.904 --> 00:37:38.865
Welcome to Portland, bitch.

00:37:40.909 --> 00:37:44.080
Well, I'll e-mail you.
Maybe I'll drop back in...

00:37:44.289 --> 00:37:46.041
...say hey.

00:37:49.629 --> 00:37:50.922
Good luck, man.

00:38:07.234 --> 00:38:09.278
Want me to take you home?

00:38:12.449 --> 00:38:15.202
I hate her so much.

00:38:15.661 --> 00:38:19.583
I mean, she tried to drive you out.
She almost destroyed my dad.

00:38:19.791 --> 00:38:22.461
She nearly killed Luke.

00:38:24.130 --> 00:38:26.258
I have to do something.

00:38:29.220 --> 00:38:30.763
Okay.

00:38:30.972 --> 00:38:32.849
So where we going?

00:38:41.402 --> 00:38:42.862
Marissa. Hello.

00:38:43.655 --> 00:38:46.241
Come in. Is everything all right?

00:38:46.825 --> 00:38:49.036
Actually, no, it's not.

00:38:49.871 --> 00:38:53.000
We need to talk about my mom.

00:38:53.458 --> 00:38:56.421
I was just thinking the same thing.
Sit down, please.

00:38:58.006 --> 00:39:00.968
I know things between you
and your mom have been rocky this year.

00:39:01.176 --> 00:39:05.766
- Can you both put the past behind you?
- You have no idea what she's like...

00:39:05.974 --> 00:39:08.227
...or what she's done.
- I know.

00:39:09.687 --> 00:39:11.231
I know.

00:39:11.398 --> 00:39:13.066
Everything.

00:39:14.485 --> 00:39:18.156
We should use this occasion
as a chance to heal.

00:39:18.949 --> 00:39:20.951
Make a fresh start.

00:39:21.452 --> 00:39:24.205
Family is very important to me, Marissa.

00:39:24.372 --> 00:39:26.834
I want us all to be a real family.

00:39:27.042 --> 00:39:30.129
- Your sister deserves that, so do you.
- We already have a dad.

00:39:30.338 --> 00:39:33.967
I'm well aware. I'm not trying
to replace him, push him out.

00:39:34.176 --> 00:39:36.763
Quite the opposite, in fact.
As of today...

00:39:36.971 --> 00:39:40.935
...I'm the only chance your father has.
- What are you talking about?

00:39:41.143 --> 00:39:43.938
This morning I offered to buy
the Balboa Lighthouse...

00:39:44.147 --> 00:39:47.568
...from both he and Sandy
for several million dollars.

00:39:49.612 --> 00:39:53.534
Considering the fact that the restaurant
will never open, make a cent...

00:39:53.742 --> 00:39:58.331
...I'd say it was a pretty good deal.
However, if I were to change my mind...

00:39:58.540 --> 00:40:01.836
...decide it was a bad investment,
lose my checkbook...

00:40:02.795 --> 00:40:04.798
...your father would be ruined.

00:40:05.966 --> 00:40:07.760
Penniless.

00:40:08.803 --> 00:40:10.513
Run out of town.

00:40:10.972 --> 00:40:12.557
Which is where I come in.

00:40:12.849 --> 00:40:14.768
You are very important to your mother.

00:40:15.311 --> 00:40:17.772
She is very important to me.

00:40:18.523 --> 00:40:21.819
- Be part of our family.
- Which means what, exactly?

00:40:22.028 --> 00:40:25.448
Well, you're already part of the wedding.
When your mom moves in...

00:40:25.657 --> 00:40:28.411
...you come and live with us too.
- You're joking, right?

00:40:28.619 --> 00:40:30.121
It would mean everything to her.

00:40:42.303 --> 00:40:46.809
And if I do this, then you'll
definitely buy the restaurant?

00:40:47.017 --> 00:40:49.687
This conversation would have
to remain confidential.

00:40:50.104 --> 00:40:54.109
You wouldn't want my mom to know
you blackmailed me into living with her?

00:41:00.993 --> 00:41:02.620
So do we have a deal?

00:41:06.750 --> 00:41:11.506
Wonderful. Now, was there something
else that you wanted to ask me about?

00:41:21.936 --> 00:41:24.940
- You okay?
- I'm a prisoner in my own life. I'm great.

00:41:25.148 --> 00:41:27.818
- Well, you did what you needed to do.
- Yeah.

00:41:27.985 --> 00:41:32.574
- I guess I just need some sleep.
- Yeah, okay. I'll call you...

00:41:33.867 --> 00:41:36.788
I told you, no touching anything, ever.

00:41:37.914 --> 00:41:40.417
- You're such a dandy, Cohen.
- You're a dandy, woman.

00:41:40.626 --> 00:41:42.295
- Fine, take it.
- No. I don't want it.

00:41:42.503 --> 00:41:44.547
Oh, my God!

00:41:59.441 --> 00:42:01.861
Those are tears of joy, yes?

00:42:04.072 --> 00:42:05.615
I...

00:42:06.074 --> 00:42:08.995
I don't even know what to say.

00:42:09.871 --> 00:42:12.040
Summer did all the building.

00:42:12.499 --> 00:42:16.045
And the heavy lifting. And the wiring
of the electronics. But I painted.

00:42:16.254 --> 00:42:18.214
I know you're a Paris fan.

00:42:18.423 --> 00:42:20.509
It's amazing.

00:42:20.718 --> 00:42:22.845
This is so cool.

00:42:23.054 --> 00:42:26.224
We looked through your toys
and couldn't find any plastic horses...

00:42:26.433 --> 00:42:29.437
...but we did find this.

00:42:29.645 --> 00:42:32.149
Share Bear! Wow!

00:42:32.357 --> 00:42:34.902
Yeah, she'll watch over you
with her Care Bear stare.

00:42:35.111 --> 00:42:36.988
How do you know
about the Care Bear stare?

00:42:37.906 --> 00:42:39.825
- I painted that.
- Yes, you did.

00:42:40.033 --> 00:42:41.660
I did.

00:42:46.375 --> 00:42:48.169
Thanks, you guys.

00:42:48.377 --> 00:42:51.131
- I really needed this.
- Yeah, it was nothing.

00:42:51.673 --> 00:42:55.720
For you.
You should see Cohen with a power saw.

00:42:55.928 --> 00:42:57.806
How do you know about
the Care Bear stare?

00:42:58.014 --> 00:43:00.142
- Dude, leave it alone.
- No, I'm just curious.

00:43:00.350 --> 00:43:03.605
- Isn't he cute?
- It's like... It's kind of...
